<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2 face=TimesNewRoman&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Digital Modulation&amp;nbsp;Tx and Rx (with&amp;nbsp;MMSE- DFE)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This workspace is to demostrate Digital Modulation&amp;nbsp;source and receiver using SystemVue data flow model and MATLAB Script model. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The source consists of Preamble and data Payload parts. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Both Preamble and data Payload part can be set as &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;BPSK, QPSK, 8-PSK, 16-QAM, 32-QAM, 64-QAM, 128-QAM, 256-QAM, 512-QAM, 1024-QAM, 2048-QAM, 4096-QAM, 16-APSK, 32-APSK, 16 Star-QAM, 32 Star-QAM and Custom APSK. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Transmit shaping filter can be selected as Raised Cosine or Root Raised Cosine. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The bandwidth is determined by the ChipRate parameter. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Oversampling ratio is determined by SampsPerChip parameter.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;In the receiver side, it consists of receiver filter (Root Raised Cosine or No), frame synchronization, automatic gain control (AGC), carrier&amp;nbsp;frequency synchronization, carrier phase estimator. The equalizer&amp;nbsp;is the fast computation MMSE Decision feedback&amp;nbsp;Equalizer. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This workspace consists of three folders (1. MMSE-DFE, 2. MMSE-DFE BER vs EbN0 and&amp;nbsp; 3. MMSE-DFE BER vs SNR). &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Folder 1. MMSE-DFE have one schematic DigMod_MMSE-DFE_TxRx and can show equalized constellation, estimated frequency offset, synchronization index EVM, BER and etc after running it.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Folder 2. MMSE-DFE BER vs EbN0 have two schematic DigMod_RFxcvr_BER and DigMod_RFxcvr_ChCoding_BER. &amp;nbsp;Both schematic can sweep EbN0, bitwidths of ADC (AtoD Analog to Digital Convertor). DigMod_RFxcvr_BER does not include channel coding and channel decoding and get raw BER (uncoded BER) and Schematic DigMod_RFxcvr_ChCoding_BER&amp;nbsp;includes channel coding and decoding (ReedSolomon Encoder (255, 240) and 1/2 convolutional coder) and can get coded BER.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Folder 3. MMSE-DFE BER vs SNR&amp;nbsp;have two schematic DigMod_RFxcvr_BER_SNR and DigMod_RFxcvr_ChCoding_BER_SNR (same as Folder 2 use SNR to replace EbN0) and can get raw BER vs SNR and coded BER vs SNR curves. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Ot14;am14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;yYmB2lG2l24;jms2SBO}b24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;;A6;q4</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>3</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr" />
<Item XName="Theoretical_256-QAM_BER" UserName="Theoretical_256-QAM_BER" Type="Equation">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>EbNodB_256=0:1:26&#x000D;&#x000A;EbNo=10.^(EbNodB_256/10);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;k=8;&#x000D;&#x000A;M=2^k;&#x000D;&#x000A;x=sqrt(3*k*EbNo/(M-1));&#x000D;&#x000A;QAM_256_Pb=(4/k)*(1-1/sqrt(M))*(1/2)*erfc(x/sqrt(2));&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;SNR_dB=EbNodB_256+10*log10(k);</Text>
<UnitUse><T>Int</T><D>2</D></UnitUse>
